  "about": "#376: a remove read from an earlier epoch's mailbox after the key change out of it changes nothing there, as any record read from another epoch's mailbox doesn't (#98), and the fold names it in stranded, with the member it would remove, while its remover and that member are both still members. A device that holds it posts it again to the current epoch's mailbox, as it does a stranded leave (#225), where it takes the member out at its own place and makes the next key change due, which must leave them out. Wraps are placeholders.",
